

titre$Daldinia 
com$
1,2 $ Pigments in KOH purple, violet, greyish or absent
1,14 $ Pigments in KOH olivaceous to green
1,15 $ Pigments in KOH yellowish to reddish brown
2,3 $ Perispore dehiscent in KOH, stromata occurring on dead wood
2,11 $ Perispore indehiscent in KOH, stromata occurring preferentially on burnt substrates
3,0 $ Stromata very small, 3-5 mm diam, ascospores 9-11 x 4.5-5.5 ?m; apparently restricted to Carpinus, known from Far East Russia $ D. singularis Ju, Vasilyeva and Rogers (3)
3,4 $ Stromata larger, with larger ascospores
4,5 $ Stromata not over 20-25 mm diam
4,6 $ Stromata usually over 25 mm diam
5,0 $ Stromata usually stipitate; ascospores 14-18 x 6.5-10 ?m; on Betulaceae $ D. decipiens Stadler & Wollweber (8, 9, 12)
5,0 $ Stromata sessile; ascospores 11-13 x 5.5-6.5 ?m; on Laurus azorica, Canary Islands $ D. palmensis Stadler, Wollweber & Tichy (10)
6,0 $ Ostioles umbilicate; ascospores 10-14 x 5-7 ?m; known from Jersey Island, on Acer $ D. vanderguchtiae Stadler, Wollweber & Briegert (10)
6,7 $ Ostioles punctate to papillate; ascospores averaging larger
7,0 $ Interior gelatinous turning conspicuously loculate upon drying; ascospores 12.5-15.5 x 6-7.5 ?m; North America (and northern Europe, unpublished) $ D. gelatinosa Ju, Rogers & San Martin (2)
7,8 $ Interior pithy, solid to rarely loculate in places
8,9 $ Stromatal surface reticulate-cracked
8,10 $ Stromatal surface not reticulate-cracked
9,0 $ Ostioles finely papillate; ascospores 13-17 x 6-7.5 ?m; plurivorous, frequent on Fraxinus, temperate Europe $ D. concentrica (Bolt.: Fr.) Ces. & De Not. (4, 5, 6, 9, 10, 12)
9,0 $ Ostioles punctate; ascospores 14-17 x 6-8 ?m; on Quercus suber and Carya olivaeformis, Sicily. $ D. martinii Stadler, Venturella & Wollweber (10)
10,0 $ Ostioles papillate ; ascospores 12.5-16.5 x 6.5-7.5 ?m; on Betulaceae, in Alps and Central Europe $ D. petriniae Ju, Rogers & San Martin [2, 4 (as D. occidentalis), 6, 9, 12]
10,0 $ Ostioles punctate ; ascospores 12-14 x 6-7 ?m ; on Quercus ilex, known from Sicily and Ile de Ré $ D. raimundii Stadler, Venturella & Wollweber (10)
10,0 $ Ostioles punctate ; ascospores 13-16 x 5-7 ?m ; on Ocotea foetens, Canary Islands, Madeira $ D. macaronesica Stadler, Wollweber & Castro (10)
11,0 $ Ascospores 8-11 x 4-5.5 ?m; most often on burnt Ulex $ D. caldariorum Henn. (2, 6, 9, 12)
11,12 $ Ascospores larger
12,0 $ Interior gelatinous, turning loculate, white, with zonation often inconspicuous at maturity; ascospores 11.5-15.5 x 6.5-9 ?m, on various burnt woody substrates including Ulex, north temperate to subtropical $ D. fissa Lloyd (2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12)
12,13 $ Interior pithy to fibrous, solid, grey brown, weakly loculate, with conspicuous zonation; on burnt wood
13,0 $ Ascospores 11-14 x 6-8 ?m ; Scandinavia, Germany and UK. $ D. loculata (Lév.) Sacc. (1, 2, 4, 6, 9, 12)
13,0 $ Ascospores 15-19 x 7-9 ?m; Canada, UK, Czech Republic $ D. loculatoides Wollweber & Stadler (11)
14,0 $ Surface of young stromata with conspicuous brown polygonal scales; pigments in KOH greenish; ascospores 12-18 x 6-7.5 ?m; on Betula $ D. lloydii Ju, Rogers & San
14,0 $ Surface lacking polygonal scales; pigments in KOH olivaceous, at times with a purplish shade; ascospores 12.5-16.5 x 6.5-7.5 ?m; on Betulaceae $ D. petriniae Ju, Rogers & San Martin [2, 4(as D. occidentalis), 6, 9, 12]
15,0 $ Stromata usually on a short stout stipe, rarely over 2 cm diam; ascospores 12-16 x 5.5-7.5 ?m; cosmopolitan in warm temperate areas $ D. childiae Rogers & Ju (5, 6, 9, 12)
15,0 $ Stromata sessile, larger; ascospores 13-17 x 6.5-8 ?m ; known from Spanish Pyrénées and Central Europe $ D. pyrenaica Stadler & Wollweber (7, 9, 12)
